  "notes": "Modified cash basis, one government-wide net position statement (p1) used for balance_sheet (Total column). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); transfers_in 25,010 is the total-column net after eliminating 53,282 of inter-governmental-fund transfers (the 25,010 comes from the Water fund, business_type transfers_net -25,010). Business-type lines from the Proprietary Funds statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p6, Totals column); measure is net position because the report presents net position for the proprietary funds; capital grants 5,200 (Garbage) go to business_type.other_financing. Reconciles: governmental 938,019 + 1,073,077 - 923,581 + 25,010 = 1,112,525; business 1,861,498 + 626,546 - 624,693 + 5,200 - 25,010 = 1,843,541. Beginning/ending governmental balances are fund balances, all cash on this basis. The p9 budgetary all-funds schedule (General All-Purpose column) combines governmental and utility funds and cannot be split by fund type, so it is not recorded in detail (statements p4/p6 cover it); only the nonmajor combining schedule (p10, 6 funds) is in detail. Cash flow statement (p7) is modified cash basis, not recorded as GAAP proprietary. Utility fund balance sheet (p5) totals differ from the government-wide business-type column (p1) because of due-to/claim-on-cash presentation; p1 used. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}